{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/935466-starting-mana-after-timeskips","id":935466,"title":"Starting Mana after Timeskips","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-21T23:27:31-07:00","id":935466,"title":"Starting Mana after Timeskips","content":"What is the starting Mana value for a character supposed to be at the beginning of a new Story and how, if at all, do dots in Hallow play into it? The book only talks about the value at the start of the Chronicle, right after character generation.<ul><li>reset to full?</li> <li>reset to equal Wisdom?</li> <li>no change, exactly as at the end of last Story?</li> <li>1d10 + Hallow?</li> </ul><br /> I was unable to find anything about this in the book. It seems like a curious oversight. I personally like the last two best because they are the most likely to put the characters in a bind, but maybe someone has a better idea or even heard from one of the writers or even Dave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T01:16:13-07:00","id":935480,"title":"","content":"I would imagine it depends on how much time has passed, rather than any arbitrary cutoff. If the new story takes place immediately after the last one for some reason, they would presumably have the mana they ended the last story with. If a significant amount of time has lapsed and they have access to some source of mana (including any tass they can requisition from their orders), there's not much reason for them to not be topped up. Whatever follows logically, in other words.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11144-grand","name":"Grand","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T02:08:09-07:00","id":935485,"title":"","content":"It's not an oversight to assume that word count can be better spent not advising STs on how to use their rational judgement to determine the availability of a resource whose default availability is set by the ST in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T05:15:03-07:00","id":935529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/935466-starting-mana-after-timeskips?p=935485#post935485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not an oversight to assume that word count can be better spent not advising STs on how to use their rational judgement to determine the availability of a resource whose default availability is set by the ST in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is more than just availability. It takes into account things like assumed expenditure and, more importantly, <i>intended game experience</i>. VtR wants even the most well-prepared and reasonable PC to sometimes start a Story hungry or even starving so there can be all sorts of delicious complications from that. Therefore you start a VtR Story with a randomised Vitae value.<br /> Besides, your word count argument is a bit overwrought. Answering this question would have been a single short sentence to give a standard baseline answer. Then ST can still deviate however they like.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T05:28:22-07:00","id":935536,"title":"","content":"If the ST is going to deviate however they want anyway then there's no need to write a sentence to tell them to deviate.<br /> <br /> If you want to start a story with mana deprived mages, then do so, you don't need anything to tell you to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T06:52:46-07:00","id":935578,"title":"","content":"A sentence saying a baseline of 1d10 + Hallow if the game expects mages to use mana a lot during downtime isn't exactly an outlandish suggestion. There's a similar discussion in VTR, as mentioned, to show that being topped off isn't the natural state of the vampire. <br /> <br /> I'd expect mages to be topped off, since they don't need to spend mana to stay alive or use blush of life to interact with old friends or the like, and oblation doesn't require hunting humans that can start to take notice if you do it too often. Given that the book doesn't discuss it, I think that may be the intention. I'd also expect it to be limited to what the hallow is capable of producing in that time and just assume oblations are successful. I'm not a big werewolf person, so I don't know, but if there are rules about time skipping and essence I imagine they would apply to mages and hallows rather well. <br /> <br /> I do think comments about doing what you want when people have questions are unhelpful, if that's the answer then why have a book in the first place?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11862-ifisa","name":"Ifisa","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T07:12:26-07:00","id":935585,"title":"","content":"It's not having questions that's the problem, it's saying that the writers neglected to put in an unnecessary thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T07:38:19-07:00","id":935595,"title":"","content":"Personally, I go with Wisdom + Hallow (or Order Status, if higher).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T08:16:09-07:00","id":935611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/935466-starting-mana-after-timeskips?p=935585#post935585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not having questions that's the problem, it's saying that the writers neglected to put in an unnecessary thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fundamentally, everything is unnecessary. You could play Mage: the Awakening without any books at all. Make up some flavour, make up some rules and have at it.<br /> Since you, I assume, still bought the book this means there must be some draw, correct? I hazard the guess for many at least some of the draw is the mechanics as designed by the Onyx Path team, including but not limited to the expansive freeform magic system. So then, if people buy RPG books at least partially for the mechanics I do not find it unreasonable to expect the book to try for some degree of comprehensiveness in mechanics, especially on an issue that other games in the setting have already raised. Of course what is and is not the core of the mechanics is debatable, but I personally think an issue that would come up in every Chronicle that goes beyond a single Story is a core enough issue to address it at least shortly. Also since mechanics are often used to carry flavour in RPGs (especially in CofD games).<br /> <br /> To clarify, I am not trying to give the design team a hard time over this. I would just like to hear what the <i>intended default gameplay experience</i> is, so that I may then decide to stick with it or deviate from it. Just the same way how can I read the section on Creative Thaumaturgy so that I may decide to stick with it or deviate from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T08:26:32-07:00","id":935617,"title":"","content":"You can assume that it's full mana or whatever. Mages and Vampires use Mana and Blood for different purposes and the &quot;mana amanagement&quot; and &quot;blood management&quot; minigames have different emphasis. For Vampires, blood is both tactical and strategical resource - everything revolves around blood, you need it to survive, and you will probably spend it every scene; getting to 0 has real consequences.<br /> <br /> For Mages, it's less strategic and much more tactical. They have so many means to get their mana back, and it's so not-needed outside of stressful situations, that long-term mana management isn't really a problem or that interesting. There are many, many ways to get mana, and often, you are not really competing with anyone for it.<br /> When you are managing mana, it's probably in context of &quot;fuck, I need to save the world, make myself sexy for the date, and record my favorite tv show back in the 1999, and world ends in 40 minutes, goddamit stupid world&quot; or something like that - which boils down to being limited by your CURRENT and MAXIMUM mana. You *could* easily refill to full, but it would take time, and pursuing mana would mean not pursuing your goals right now.<br /> Basically, you are expected to manage Mana tactically - in context of your current &quot;encounters&quot; and chapters - and while you don't need ANY mana for everyday, off screen business, you can go dry very, very quickly during tense situations. Imagine a scene where each turn, your character is exposed to a dangerous tilt or condition that needs to be Pattern Restored ASAP. Pattern Restoration takes 3 mana. It will drain you to 0 in *4 turns* from maximum.<br /> Honestly? If you want characters in a bind, reset their Mana to maximum, but present time sensitive, mana intensive challenges. Hallows real strength isn't recharging mana when you are safe and don't have pressing matters. It's the fact that you can harvest it and store for later, when you need MANA RIGHT HERE, RIGHT NOW.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 07-22-2016, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T10:16:50-07:00","id":935665,"title":"","content":"I tend toward &quot;unless a character has no Hallow, no Legacy, and no Order status, it's full at the start of a Story.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T11:36:56-07:00","id":935714,"title":"","content":"Considering every Mage can Pattern Scour for 3 Mana <i>at least</i> every other day (more if they want to degrade a combination of Attributes and Health, and/or have quickened healing), I don't see even Mages without a Hallow, Tass, or Legacy being without Mana for long if they want it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T11:57:29-07:00","id":935724,"title":"","content":"They can also pursue their Obsessions for Mana, ask their Order nicely using free Order Status dot, go around Unveiling and Knowing with their Praxes for Exceptional Successes (this is even more efficient if does so pursues your Obsession!), and in general, search for Supernal Revelations. Or use one of many Mana Engines (though these tend risk Wisdom).<br /> These things are easy, they are exciting, and they definitely won't help you when you have 30 minutes to figure out how to send ET (Exterminating Terrestrials horror) home safely after spending your mana bank on surviving the initial encounter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T09:19:22-07:00","id":936571,"title":"","content":"Realistically, you can be worried about Mana only <i>until</i> they get Legacy. When they get one and there is any other downtime more than 72 hours - they can start at full Mana pool. They just generate any Mana needed by Legacies Oblations each day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T07:45:19-07:00","id":937083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/935466-starting-mana-after-timeskips?p=935665#post935665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend toward &quot;unless a character has no Hallow, no Legacy, and no Order status, it's full at the start of a Story.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Very Harry Dresden of you! Butcher usually starts off a book with his protagonist fully rested and charged up, possibly just to make the severe beatings he inflicts upon the poor sap that much more profound. The exceptions occur when the previous beating achieved some sort of pinnacle of transformation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6770-midgardener","name":"Midgardener","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6770_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T22:19:53-07:00","id":937485,"title":"","content":"I'd say if the players are well equipped with Hallows and haven't been especially active in the downtime then you might want to give them a small store of Tass as well at the start of the next story. (Maybe equal to the dots in the Hallow rating?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}